Modifications relative to upstream reinstall
---------------------------------------------
1. Rebranded to "Rntech": script names (rntech-install.sh, rntech-setup.bat),
   job-env field names (RNTECH_* instead of the upstream names), and guest
   paths (C:\Rntech).
2. SHA-256 verification of reinstall.sh before chmod/execute. TLS is always
   verified (no --insecure). The Windows ISO is passed to reinstall as an
   HTTP(S) URL (RNTECH_ISO_URL, validated to be http/https); reinstall fetches
   it directly inside its Alpine stage. (An earlier design pre-downloaded the
   ISO locally and passed a file:// path; that does not work because reinstall
   reboots into a fresh Alpine ramdisk and its aria2 downloader rejects
   file://.)
3. Identity-bound fresh-VPS guard: the destructive write is refused unless
   RNTECH_ALLOW_DISK_WIPE=1 AND the droplet's own cloud-metadata id
   (http://169.254.169.254/metadata/v1/id) exactly equals
   RNTECH_EXPECTED_PROVIDER_ID AND no /root/.rntech-installed marker exists.
4. RDP credentials are never placed on a command line. The RDP username and
   password (the latter base64-decoded from RNTECH_RDP_PASSWORD_B64) are fed to
   reinstall's interactive prompts over STDIN, so the password never appears as
   a process argument.

5. The install script explicitly reboots into the installer environment after
   reinstall stages the GRUB entry, and posts installing/finishing/done/failed
   callbacks to the panel.

